<section class="section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
  <div class="section__head">
    <div>
      <h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <p>Quick answers about this mirror list and how status checks work.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="faq">
    <details open>
      <summary>Is GKStreams down right now?</summary>
      <p>
        Check the mirror cards above. Each domain shows LIVE or DOWN and is re-checked
        every 5 minutes. If every mirror is DOWN, wait a few minutes and refresh —
        temporary outages are shown automatically when a mirror recovers.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>What is a GKStreams mirror?</summary>
      <p>
        A mirror is an alternate address for the same service, used when the primary
        domain is unavailable. This landing page only <strong>lists</strong> those
        addresses. It does not host streams, embed players, or store any media.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>How often is status updated?</summary>
      <p>
        Automated checks run every 5 minutes from an external cron job. The page is
        rebuilt with the latest LIVE/DOWN state, and a small script can refresh badges
        from <code>/status.json</code> without reloading.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Does this website host any streams?</summary>
      <p>
        No. This is an informational directory only. There is no video, audio, embed,
        or playback functionality on this domain. Links go to third-party sites we do
        not control. See our <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer and DMCA policy</a>.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Why do I see different results than before?</summary>
      <p>
        Network conditions change. A host may be temporarily unreachable from the
        checker’s network while still working for you — or the reverse. Try another
        LIVE mirror if one fails.
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
